From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hexdump <hexdump0815@googlemail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Feb 2025 09:42:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add the Samsung Galaxy Book Go

Add the Samsung Galaxy Book Go (NP340XLA Wi-Fi, NP345XLA LTE), a
Snapdragon 7c Gen 2 laptop. The tree started from the Acer Aspire 1
tree, with the keyboard, touchpad, bridge bus, UFS and microSD moved
to where the Galaxy Book Go has them.

[birk: the draft from misc.qc7/misc/sc7180-samsung-galaxy-book-go.draft
at 148a96083d30 (BSD-3-Clause, as its SPDX line says), with every board
value checked against Samsung's DSDT (aarch64-laptops/build
misc/samsung-galaxy-book-go). The DSDT's I2C1, I2C5, I2C7, IC10 and
IC11 sit at 0x880000, 0x890000, 0xa80000, 0xa8c000 and 0xa90000, which
are i2c0, i2c4, i2c6, i2c9 and i2c10. GpioInt pins of 0x140 and up are
GIO0's direct interrupts, whose PDC pins sc7180_pdc_map turns into TLMM
GPIOs. xbill9 dumped the same tables from an NP340XLA and tested most of
the fixes below on it (github.com/xbill9/linux-arm-adventures,
galaxy-book-go/).

What the DSDT gives, and where it differs from the draft, is below.

- The keyboard (ECKB, SSEC0001) is at 0x05 on i2c6 with its HID
  descriptor at 0x20, and its GpioInt is direct interrupt 5, PDC 67,
  TLMM 104, level low with a pull-up. The draft's GPIO 48 is the USB
  function's GpioIo (URS0.UFN0) and idles low, so i2c-hid polled the
  keyboard about 1100 times a second. That flood is the flaky keyboard
  owners reported.
- The touchpad (TCPD, SSTP0001) is at 0x40 on i2c10, descriptor 0x0e,
  interrupt on direct interrupt 6, TLMM 31, with a pull-up. Its PEP
  entry (TPXC) drives GPIO 32 high, votes LDO10_A at 1.8 V and waits
  150 ms, as the draft has it.
- The bridge (GPU0's I2C resources) is the SN65DSI86 at 0x2c on i2c0
  with its reference clock on BBCLK3. The DSDT gives it no interrupt,
  and the Samsung EC device (EMEC) reads GPIO 11, 19, 22 and 51 as
  inputs, so the Aspire 1's interrupt on 11, enable on 51, suspend on 22
  and 1.2 V switch on 19 go. The 1.8 V switch on GPIO 20 goes too, since
  GPIO 20 is one of the two outputs Samsung's audio device (AUDD)
  declares. GPU0's power-up turns on LDO8_C and LDO13_A at 1.8 V, so
  both stay on. The GPIOs it raises next (28, 29, 37 and 2) and the
  panel reset (GPIO 36) have no role the tables name, and Linux leaves
  them as the firmware set them.
- The backlight is PWM from the PM6150L's LPG, which the panel
  configuration in GPU0._ROM selects (PMIC 2, 9 bits at 6250 Hz, so a
  160 us period). xbill9 found it on channel 4 by driving each channel
  and watching the screen.
- The smart battery gauge answers at 0x0b on i2c4, where EMEC lists 0x0b
  and the charger at 0x09 at 100 kHz. xbill9 bound sbs-battery to it.
- The lid switch is GPIO 93 (GIO0's LIDR, 1 when open), which GIO0 also
  takes as a wake event.
- The camera sits on port 4 of the internal hub, and EHUB._PS0 powers it
  through GPIO 13 (GIO0's CAME). A hog keeps it on.
- The headset codec (RTK0, ALC5682) is at 0x1a on i2c9 with its
  interrupt on direct interrupt 4, TLMM 43, pulled down. Its PEP entry
  raises GPIO 58, waits 30 ms and votes LDO15_A. GPIO 58 is in the
  place the Aspire 1's codec 3.3 V switch (GPIO 83) has in the Aspire's
  own PEP entry, so it feeds MICVDD and VBAT the same way.
- The speaker amplifier has no device in the DSDT. AUDD drives GPIO 21
  and 20 and votes BOB at 3.296 V. Samsung's audio calibration puts the
  speakers on tertiary MI2S and the headset on primary MI2S, and xbill9
  measured the speaker data on sd line 1. The tree keeps BOB on at
  3.296 V, uses GPIO 21 as the amplifier's SD_MODE and holds GPIO 20
  high, as the draft did through its bridge supply.
- The ADSP image Samsung ships spans 0x2e00000, more than the Aspire's
  0x2800000, so adsp_mem grows to fit it.
- The microSD card detect is direct interrupt 3, TLMM 69, with LDO9_C
  and LDO6_C. UFS takes LDO19_A, LDO12_A, LDO3_C and LDO4_A, USB takes
  LDO11_A, LDO17_A, LDO3_C and LDO4_A, and Bluetooth takes LDO1_C,
  LDO2_C and LDO10_C, as in the draft.
- The PEP configures every I2C bus's pins with the internal pull-up at
  2 mA, not the Aspire's 16 mA without pull.
- The power key is the PMIC's (BTNS on PM01 pin 0), so pon stays on.

The Aspire 1's RTS5411 hub nodes go as well, since the internal
hub is a four-port USB 2.0 hub (EHUB) that owners see as 0424:2514. The
draft's i2c2, i2c5 and i2c7 go, as they hold only the EC, the Wi-Fi SAR
sensor and an EC touchpad device (ECTC) that Linux has no driver for.
The firmware moves to qcom/sc7180/Samsung/galaxy-book-go, and the nodes
use 7.3's labels.

The RTC stays off, since its counter reads 1970 and the firmware keeps
its offset elsewhere. The charger, a BQ25710 at 0x09 that stops charging
175 s after its last write, needs a driver. USB-C orientation and
DisplayPort need the EC's connector, so USB-C works only if plugged at
boot. The LTE modem needs the full modem image and IPA, so both models
load the Wi-Fi-only modem image.]
Link: https://github.com/hexdump0815/linux-mainline-qcom-kernel/blob/148a96083d30/misc.qc7/misc/sc7180-samsung-galaxy-book-go.draft
Link: https://github.com/xbill9/linux-arm-adventures/tree/main/galaxy-book-go
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../qcom/sc7180-samsung-galaxy-book-go.dts    | 920 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 920 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-samsung-galaxy-book-go.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-samsung-galaxy-book-go.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-samsung-galaxy-book-go.dts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f178adb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180-samsung-galaxy-book-go.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,920 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * Samsung Galaxy Book Go (NP340XLA Wi-Fi, NP345XLA LTE)
+ *
+ * Snapdragon 7c Gen 2 clamshell. Started from the Acer Aspire 1 tree;
+ * the board values are the ones Samsung's DSDT gives: the SN65DSI86
+ * bridge on i2c0, the keyboard on i2c6, the touchpad on i2c10, the
+ * headset codec on i2c9, the smart battery on i2c4, UFS storage and a
+ * microSD slot.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/gpio-keys.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6asm.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/regulator/qcom,rpmh-regulator.h>
+
+#include "sc7180.dtsi"
+
+#include "pm6150.dtsi"
+#include "pm6150l.dtsi"
+
+/delete-node/ &tz_mem;
+/delete-node/ &ipa_fw_mem;
+
+/ {
+	model = "Samsung Galaxy Book Go";
+	compatible = "samsung,galaxy-book-go", "qcom,sc7180";
+	chassis-type = "laptop";
+
+	aliases {
+		bluetooth0 = &bluetooth;
+		hsuart0 = &uart3;
+		wifi0 = &wifi;
+	};
+
+	reserved-memory {
+		gpu_mem: zap-shader@80840000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x80840000 0 0x2000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		venus_mem: venus@85b00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x85b00000 0 0x500000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		mpss_mem: mpss@86000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x86000000 0x0 0x2000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		/* Samsung's qcadsp7180.mbn spans 0x2e00000 */
+		adsp_mem: adsp@8e400000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x8e400000 0x0 0x2e00000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		wlan_mem: wlan@93900000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x93900000 0x0 0x200000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
+	max98357a: audio-codec {
+		compatible = "maxim,max98357a";
+		sdmode-gpios = <&tlmm 21 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&amp_sd_mode_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
+	};
+
+	backlight: backlight {
+		compatible = "pwm-backlight";
+		pwms = <&pm6150l_lpg 3 160000>;
+	};
+
+	gpio-keys {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&lid_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		switch-lid {
+			label = "Lid";
+			gpios = <&tlmm 93 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
+			linux,code = <SW_LID>;
+			wakeup-source;
+			wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	reg_codec_3p3: codec-regulator {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "codec_3p3";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 58 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		startup-delay-us = <30000>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&reg_audio_en_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+
+	sound: sound {
+		compatible = "qcom,sc7180-qdsp6-sndcard";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pri_mi2s_active>, <&pri_mi2s_mclk_active>, <&ter_mi2s_active>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		model = "Samsung-Galaxy-Book-Go";
+
+		audio-routing =
+			"Headphone Jack", "HPOL",
+			"Headphone Jack", "HPOR";
+
+		multimedia1-dai-link {
+			link-name = "MultiMedia1";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA1>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		multimedia2-dai-link {
+			link-name = "MultiMedia2";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA2>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		multimedia3-dai-link {
+			link-name = "MultiMedia3";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA3>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		multimedia4-dai-link {
+			link-name = "MultiMedia4";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA4>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		primary-rx-dai-link {
+			link-name = "Primary MI2S Playback";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6afedai PRIMARY_MI2S_RX>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&alc5682 0>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		primary-tx-dai-link {
+			link-name = "Primary MI2S Capture";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6afedai PRIMARY_MI2S_TX>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&alc5682 0>;
+			};
+		};
+
+		tertiary-rx-dai-link {
+			link-name = "Tertiary MI2S Playback";
+
+			cpu {
+				sound-dai = <&q6afedai TERTIARY_MI2S_RX>;
+			};
+
+			platform {
+				sound-dai = <&q6routing>;
+			};
+
+			codec {
+				sound-dai = <&max98357a>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
+	vdd_touchpad: touchpad-regulator {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vdd_touchpad";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 32 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&reg_tp_en_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+	};
+};
+
+&gpu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&gpu_zap_shader {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/Samsung/galaxy-book-go/qcdxkmsuc7180.mbn";
+};
+
+&i2c0 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	sn65dsi86_bridge: bridge@2c {
+		compatible = "ti,sn65dsi86";
+		reg = <0x2c>;
+		gpio-controller;
+		#gpio-cells = <2>;
+		#pwm-cells = <1>;
+
+		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_LN_BB_CLK3>;
+		clock-names = "refclk";
+
+		ports {
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+
+			port@0 {
+				reg = <0>;
+
+				sn65dsi86_in: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&mdss_dsi0_out>;
+				};
+			};
+
+			port@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+
+				sn65dsi86_out: endpoint {
+					data-lanes = <0 1>;
+					remote-endpoint = <&panel_in_edp>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
+		aux-bus {
+			panel: panel {
+				compatible = "edp-panel";
+				backlight = <&backlight>;
+
+				port {
+					panel_in_edp: endpoint {
+						remote-endpoint = <&sn65dsi86_out>;
+					};
+				};
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c4 {
+	clock-frequency = <100000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	battery@b {
+		compatible = "sbs,sbs-battery";
+		reg = <0xb>;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c6 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	keyboard@5 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x5>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x20>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 104 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&hid_keyboard_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c9 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	alc5682: codec@1a {
+		compatible = "realtek,rt5682i";
+		reg = <0x1a>;
+
+		#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
+
+		interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
+		interrupts = <43 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&codec_irq_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		AVDD-supply = <&vreg_l15a_1p8>;
+		MICVDD-supply = <&reg_codec_3p3>;
+		VBAT-supply = <&reg_codec_3p3>;
+		DBVDD-supply = <&vreg_l15a_1p8>;
+		LDO1-IN-supply = <&vreg_l15a_1p8>;
+
+		realtek,jd-src = <1>;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c10 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	touchpad@40 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x40>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x0e>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 31 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&hid_touchpad_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		vdd-supply = <&vdd_touchpad>;
+		vddl-supply = <&vreg_l10a_1p8>;
+		post-power-on-delay-ms = <150>;
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+};
+
+&mdss {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdss_dsi0 {
+	vdda-supply = <&vreg_l3c_1p2>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdss_dsi0_out {
+	remote-endpoint = <&sn65dsi86_in>;
+	data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
+};
+
+&mdss_dsi0_phy {
+	vdds-supply = <&vreg_l4a_0p8>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&pm6150_adc {
+	channel@4e {
+		reg = <ADC5_AMUX_THM2_100K_PU>;
+		qcom,ratiometric;
+		qcom,hw-settle-time = <200>;
+		label = "thermistor";
+	};
+
+	channel@4f {
+		reg = <ADC5_AMUX_THM3_100K_PU>;
+		qcom,ratiometric;
+		qcom,hw-settle-time = <200>;
+		label = "charger_thermistor";
+	};
+};
+
+&pm6150_adc_tm {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	charger-thermistor@0 {
+		reg = <0>;
+		io-channels = <&pm6150_adc ADC5_AMUX_THM3_100K_PU>;
+		qcom,ratiometric;
+		qcom,hw-settle-time-us = <200>;
+	};
+
+	thermistor@1 {
+		reg = <1>;
+		io-channels = <&pm6150_adc ADC5_AMUX_THM2_100K_PU>;
+		qcom,ratiometric;
+		qcom,hw-settle-time-us = <200>;
+	};
+};
+
+&pm6150l_lpg {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&q6afedai {
+	dai@16 {
+		reg = <PRIMARY_MI2S_RX>;
+		qcom,sd-lines = <1>;
+	};
+
+	dai@17 {
+		reg = <PRIMARY_MI2S_TX>;
+		qcom,sd-lines = <0>;
+	};
+
+	dai@20 {
+		reg = <TERTIARY_MI2S_RX>;
+		qcom,sd-lines = <1>;
+	};
+};
+
+&q6asmdai {
+	dai@0 {
+		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA1>;
+	};
+
+	dai@1 {
+		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA2>;
+	};
+
+	dai@2 {
+		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA3>;
+	};
+
+	dai@3 {
+		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA4>;
+	};
+};
+
+&qupv3_id_0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&qupv3_id_1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	memory-region = <&adsp_mem>;
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/Samsung/galaxy-book-go/qcadsp7180.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&remoteproc_mpss {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/Samsung/galaxy-book-go/qcmpss7180_nm.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&sdhc_2 {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&sdc2_on>;
+	pinctrl-1 = <&sdc2_off>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
+	vmmc-supply = <&vreg_l9c_2p9>;
+	vqmmc-supply = <&vreg_l6c_2p9>;
+
+	cd-gpios = <&tlmm 69 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&uart3 {
+	/delete-property/interrupts;
+	interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 604 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			      <&tlmm 41 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+
+	pinctrl-1 = <&qup_uart3_sleep>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	bluetooth: bluetooth {
+		compatible = "qcom,wcn3991-bt";
+		vddio-supply = <&vreg_l10a_1p8>;
+		vddxo-supply = <&vreg_l1c_1p8>;
+		vddrf-supply = <&vreg_l2c_1p3>;
+		vddch0-supply = <&vreg_l10c_3p3>;
+		max-speed = <3200000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&ufs_mem_hc {
+	vcc-supply = <&vreg_l19a_2p9>;
+	vcc-max-microamp = <600000>;
+	vccq2-supply = <&vreg_l12a_1p8>;
+	vccq2-max-microamp = <600000>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ufs_mem_phy {
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l4a_0p8>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l3c_1p2>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_1_dwc3 {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+};
+
+&usb_1_hsphy {
+	vdd-supply = <&vreg_l4a_0p8>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l11a_1p8>;
+	vdda-phy-dpdm-supply = <&vreg_l17a_3p0>;
+	qcom,imp-res-offset-value = <8>;
+	qcom,preemphasis-level = <QUSB2_V2_PREEMPHASIS_15_PERCENT>;
+	qcom,preemphasis-width = <QUSB2_V2_PREEMPHASIS_WIDTH_HALF_BIT>;
+	qcom,bias-ctrl-value = <0x22>;
+	qcom,charge-ctrl-value = <3>;
+	qcom,hsdisc-trim-value = <0>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_1_qmpphy {
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l4a_0p8>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l3c_1p2>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&venus {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sc7180/Samsung/galaxy-book-go/qcvss7180.mbn";
